 #:seon.task{:name "install-row-throws-are-not-attributed-to-a-caller-or-an-error-record"
             :plan "Health at fanout-2 (default 795a770c2, three model agents) showed `seon.sci.eval/install-row!` thrown 1,588 times; on the next JVM (HEAD, 2026-10-09, one hour after boot) the profile cell showed 34,051 entries and 3,152 clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo throws with an EMPTY error store (no :seon.error/* fact, `seon.problems/open-faults` empty), so none was recorded or delivered. Ordinary agent eval requests do NOT throw it (scratch agent: defn, redefinition, require, deftest + redefinition, fresh-agent acquisition, a schema-less defn refused at derive: 0 throws in all, 20+ install-row! entries). The throws correlate 1:1 with test-run traffic: seon.test/run-request, seon.test.runner/run-var!, seon.test-support/reply and seon.cluster.agent/release-context! each show ~1,430-1,540 throws, seon.cluster.registry/retire-branch! 1,523, seon.config/effective 2,822 and seon.fault/fault! 2,834 (about two per test run), i.e. a test (or the same few tests re-run each pass: see seon.test/a-timed-out-unrelated-test-restarts-in-every-eval-request) throws through install-row! on each run. Its callers catch Throwable in `seon.sci.eval/install-selected!` (acquisition-refusal, recorded by `record-acquisition-refusals!`) or in the test harness; the profile cell counts only the class, not the message. Done when (1) the profile throw cell names the exception message class of its top throw (or the producer is found and its message is shown by an assertion), (2) the test run that throws is identified by name and either fixed or its throw is an expected refusal returned as data, and (3) after a full eval-request sequence on a fresh JVM the install-row! throw count is 0 unless an error record with its task exists. Read `seon.profile/cells`."}
