             :plan "On default HEAD f54e73c83 (2026-10-09) the second and later `(+ 1 2)` of one branch agent through MCP sci each answered `:seon.cost/calls` 53,428-53,514 armed calls in 61-95 ms (fork 12-18 ms, test-step 13-18 ms, settle 27-36 ms); `seon.instrument/hot-internals-pay-armed-validation` measured about 6,600 per trivial form earlier. A JVM-wide counter window over one such request (other agents active) ranked `seon.sci.eval/own-binding?` 31,703 calls, `seon.sci.eval/sci-var?` 31,703 and `seon.sci.eval/ctx?` 32,003: a per-Var walk of the whole namespace state (`seon.sci.eval/regenerate-agent-context!` and `seon.sci.eval/turn-interns` call `own-binding?` per Var). Confirm the attribution inside the request's own call sink, then make the walk proportional to the Vars the context wrote, not to every Var, so a trivial form costs a few thousand armed calls. Read `seon.sci.eval/fork-for-turn`."} #:seon.task{:name "a-fork-snapshots-every-program-var"
