 #:seon.task{:name "contract-context-projection"
             :plan "Give `seon.sci.eval/context-projection` a complete Malli contract that checks what its boundary is for, with the cheapest schema that checks it: registered names, every input and output, the error variants it returns. A contract that refuses a real value (a reaching test, a live call, your probe) is a finding, not friction: if the contract misread the value's shape, fix the contract and cite the observed shape; if the producer emits a bad value, keep the contract, send root the finding with `my.message/send`, naming `seon.sci.eval/context-projection` with the exact form, the refused value's essence and the Malli explain, and say so in your reply. Never widen to :any, [:maybe ...] or :map to go green. Done when `seon.contracts/gaps` answers [] for it and its reaching tests stay green and no slower. Read `docs/seon/architecture/contracts-guide.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-ns-form-at-the-repl-only-accretes-requires"
             :plan "An `ns` form or `require` evaluated at the REPL edits the stored ns text by `seon.sci.eval/declared-source`, which appends added libspecs and strips removed aliases but never removes a require: adding `[seon.profile :as profile]`, then re-evaluating the ns form with `[seon.profile]` and then the original form left `[seon.profile]` twice in `seon.error-test`'s stored `:seon.ns/source` (2026-10-10). The branch's ns row can then never equal the file again, so `seon.cluster.branch-evidence/branch-evidence` refuses the file and the agent must restart on a fresh branch. Done when re-evaluating a namespace's ns form makes its stored source declare exactly that form's requires. Read `seon.sci.eval/namespace-source`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-alias-required-at-the-repl-is-missing-when-a-test-row-installs"
             :plan "A test defined at the REPL after `(require '[seon.profile :as profile])` in `seon.error-test` runs at the REPL but errors under `my.test/check` with \"The admitted identity has no executable test Var.\": `seon.sci.eval/interpret-test!`-style row installation refuses the row (`seon.sci.eval/acquisition-refusal`), although the ns entity lists the alias; the fully qualified `seon.profile/calls-of` installs. The recorded error carries neither the row nor the cause message (`:seon.sci.eval/acquisition-observation` and `:seon.error/data` are absent from the stored error), so the agent cannot see why (error 500ddeeeca09, 2026-10-10). Done when a test using a REPL-added alias installs in the runner, and a refused row's stored error names the row and its cause. Read `seon.sci.eval/record-acquisition-refusals!` and `seon.test/resolve-test`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-test-namespace-an-agent-requires-is-interpreted-not-host-loaded"
             :plan "An agent's `(require 'seon.id-test)` or `in-ns` into a test namespace runs `seon.sci.eval/enter-namespace!`, whose `seon.sci.eval/host-namespace!` does `require :reload` in the shared JVM; running the deftest then resolves it through `seon.test/resolve-test`, whose `seon.test/resolve-loaded` loads it again as a host Var (and `seon.sci.eval/interpret-test!` also needs the host namespace loaded). Observed on default 18919b663 as agent sci-tests, 2026-10-10: `(find-ns 'seon.id-test)` was nil in the JVM before the agent's require and run, and present after. Owner ruling (2026-10-09, restated 2026-10-10): an agent's test namespaces are interpreted from their program rows in its SCI world and never loaded into the shared JVM. Done when entering a namespace of the test source root interprets its function and test rows (`seon.sci.eval/install-selected!`) without `seon.sci.eval/host-namespace!`, `seon.test/resolve-test` resolves a test of that root from the member context, the JVM holds no namespace of it afterwards, and a branch redefinition of the subject changes the test's result. Blocked by `seon.sci.eval/sci-binding-of-a-host-dynamic-var-never-reaches-host-code`. Read `seon.sci.eval/agent-require`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "sci-binding-of-a-host-dynamic-var-never-reaches-host-code"
             :plan "A host dynamic Var copied into SCI by `seon.sci.eval/copy-host-var` (`sci.core/copy-var*`) is a separate SCI Var: SCI's `binding` pushes only the SCI Var, so compiled code reading the host Var never sees it. Agent sci-tests on default, 2026-10-10: `(binding [*print-length* 2] (.deref (clojure.lang.Var/find 'clojure.core/*print-length*)))` answered nil, and `(binding [seon.db/*read-evidence-sink* :probe] (.deref (clojure.lang.Var/find 'seon.db/*read-evidence-sink*)))` answered the host root atom, not :probe. An interpreted test (73 test files use `binding`, e.g. `seon.test-support/run-database-body` binds `seon.db/*read-evidence-sink*` around host reads) therefore runs differently from its compiled form, which blocks interpreting test namespaces in SCI. Done when SCI `binding` of a copied host dynamic Var also binds the host Var for the extent (our SCI fork, `sci.impl.vars/push-thread-bindings`), proven by the two forms above answering the bound values. Read `sci.core/binding`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-non-root-agent-never-loads-into-the-shared-jvm"
             :plan "Owner, 2026-10-10: a non-root agent never loads, reloads or interns anything in the JVM every cluster shares; only root's adoption after a merge changes the host. Paths found in a clj-kondo analysis of src (requires, loads, interns, requiring-resolve and eval whose target an agent controls): `seon.sci.eval/enter-namespace!` through `seon.sci.eval/host-namespace!` (an agent's require or in-ns of a test namespace, or of one the JVM never loaded); `seon.test/resolve-test` through `seon.test/resolve-loaded`, plus `seon.test/arm-first-loads!` (every test run); `seon.turn.batch/jvm-evaluate` (MCP jvm mode, any agent); and `seon.schedule/invoke-handler` (requiring-resolve of a stored handler symbol). SCI's own `require :reload` and `load-string` stay inside SCI: agent sci-tests' `(require 'seon.sci.forgive :reload)` left the host Var root of `seon.sci.forgive/segments` unchanged on default a6cbe4fcf. Done when a non-root agent's SCI `require :reload` and require of a test namespace leave the host's namespaces and Vars unchanged, and its jvm-mode request is refused by name. Read `seon.sci.eval/source-namespace?` and `seon.turn.batch/jvm-request`."}
