 #:seon.task{:name "a-context-holds-the-basis-it-acquired-not-the-database-value"
             :plan "A context's program snapshot holds whole database values for its life: `:seon.db/db` (set by `seon.sci.eval/acquire!`, `seon.sci.eval/copy-base-ctx` and installation settlement) and `:seon.sci.eval/loaded-database` (a `datahike.api/commit-as-db` of the loaded source commit). A retention collection reclaims the nodes of any value no branch head reaches, so a later read of a held value answers \"Node not found in storage.\": on 2026-10-11 every eval request on default failed that way until a restart, through `seon.sci.eval/acquired-database?` reading the held value's index (fixed there; proof `seon.cluster.armed-test/an-eval-request-after-a-collection-reads-no-collected-value`). Done when the snapshot holds the acquired basis as data (commit id and `seon.sci.eval/program-revisions`) and every reader opens the value it needs from its connection (`seon.sci.eval/loaded-source` for the loaded program), so no context or execution handle keeps a database value across eval requests. Read `seon.cluster.agent/acquire-context!`, `seon.sci.eval/acquired-program`, `seon.sci.eval/base-ctx` and `seon.sci.eval/loaded-program`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-second-acquisition-of-an-unmoved-branch-interprets-nothing"
             :plan "Card R4. After 0c3916000 cached the overlay plan, `seon.sci.eval/interpret-overlay!` still re-interprets a branch's changed definitions on every acquisition whose commit differs from the loaded one. Cache the interpreted fork as a seon.cache kind keyed [cluster-base-key, program basis], weighed like the base, copied from (never shared live, contexts hold atoms); a second acquisition of a branch whose program did not move interprets nothing. The resume-to-a-commit path is `seon.cluster.registry/fork!` from the commit id handed datahike.api/commit-as-db (design-probes P2: 64 ms, the fork's t repeats main's, so key by commit id) plus this cache. Proofs: a cost assertion in seon.sci.acquisition-cost-test, and R1's lightness proof (start one agent under a second and 300 MB) under budget on a branch with changed definitions. Read `seon.sci.eval/base-ctx`, `seon.sci.eval/program-revisions`, `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/design-probes.md` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/runtime-follows-db.md`. Moot under the content-addressed runtime (AGENTS.md, The program is entities; owner 2026-10-19); retire when runtime-wire lands, unless its proof still fails then."}
